From d4342469d57c6fc71c9f340cdfbf3a20405a20b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:48:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix store open/close, pill/login fonts, replace live map with
 ETA detail page, add OTP debug endpoint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Store dashboard:
   - OPEN/CLOSED badge is now tappable and calls PATCH /store/profile to
     actually toggle is_open (previously display-only, so a closed store
     had no way to start accepting orders again).
   - Fixed customer-side wiring gap: orders that land in NO_STORE_AVAILABLE
     (no open store in that pincode when the order was placed) had no
     label/color on the customer Orders list and stayed stuck under
     "Active" forever. Added the status label, moved it under the
     Cancelled tab, and added an explanatory note.

2. Store products screen:
   - categoryText/categorySelectText pills had no fontFamily at all, so
     unselected pills rendered in the phone's system font instead of Inter.
   - Fixed products not appearing after being added: Add navigates to a
     separate AddProductScreen which goBack()s on success, but the screen
     stayed on the "Universal Products" tab where the new custom product
     isn't listed. Now auto-switches to "My Products" on return.

3. Login screen: every text style used bare fontWeight with no fontFamily
   import at all, so the whole screen (including "Sign in to your account"
   and "Don't have an account? Create Account") rendered in the system
   font instead of Inter. Now uses fontFamily weight variants throughout.

4. Removed the live MapView/GPS-polling screen (customer-facing order
   tracking) and replaced it with a proper order detail page:
   - New JinniETAFlight component: a themed "magic carpet" ETA visual
     (RN Animated + react-native-svg, no new dependency) replacing the map,
     with ETA estimated from pickup/destination distance (haversine),
     bucketed to a 15-45 min range.
   - Rider card now shows name, phone (call button) and rating
     (DeliveryAgentProfile.rating, new column via migration 0014).
   - The Orders tab previously had nowhere to navigate to — wrapped it in
     a new OrdersStack (OrderHistoryScreen -> OrderTracking) so tapping an
     in-progress order actually opens this detail page instead of just
     expanding inline.
   - Removed the unused duplicate modules/food/screens/OrderTrackingScreen.tsx
     (dead code, also map-based).
   - Delivery partner's own screen (DeliveryActiveOrderScreen) was already
     map-free and deep-links to Google/Apple Maps for directions — left
     as-is per request.

5. Delivery OTP debug: the OTP was already logged when OTP_DEBUG=true, but
   only after WhatsApp/SMS sends that could throw first. Moved the log
   earlier and added GET /orders/{id}/delivery-otp/debug (404s when
   OTP_DEBUG=false, so this is inert in production) so the plaintext OTP
   can be read back during local testing without digging through server
   logs or configuring WhatsApp/SMS.
